        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-08T05:38:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>TheJayMann has it right - you may CHOOSE to put cards beneath Omni-Cannon, as is listed on the card, and you never have to use a power, just because you have access to it.  Therefore, the cannon can be powered up over multiple turns for additional damage.</p>\n<p>Thanks for your question!</p>",
